# Normalize to LF inside the repository; let Git decide the working-tree form
# for ordinary text. Anything below that overrides this does so deliberately.
* text=auto

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Dillen authoring sources -- ALWAYS LF in the working tree.
#
# This is a correctness requirement, not style. A Package's `content_digest`
# is a SHA-256 over the raw bytes of its source files
# (kernel/package_content_digest.cpp). If a checkout on one platform produced
# CRLF and another LF, the same commit would compute two different digests and
# the Package would be rejected as tampered on one of them. Pinning eol=lf
# makes the digest, the Source Lock fingerprint and the Ruleset Fingerprint
# identical on every platform.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.dpackage    text eol=lf
*.dcapability text eol=lf
*.dcomponent  text eol=lf
*.dentity     text eol=lf
*.drelation   text eol=lf
# Not covered by *.drelation -- gitattributes globs are exact, so ".drelationdef"
# was falling through to `* text=auto` and picking up CRLF on any Windows clone
# with core.autocrlf=true. That is the exact defect this section exists to
# prevent, surviving in the one authoring extension that was left off the list.
*.drelationdef text eol=lf
# The bulk forms. These are GENERATED, so nothing reviews them line by
# line and a CRLF checkout would be invisible until the Package failed its
# own content digest on the platform that did not generate it.
*.dentitytable   text eol=lf
*.drelationtable text eol=lf
*.dmechanism  text eol=lf
*.dalgorithm  text eol=lf
*.ddefinition text eol=lf
*.dspawn      text eol=lf
*.druleset    text eol=lf

# Command streams are read by the CLI and compared in probes.
*.txt         text eol=lf

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Source and project files
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.c      text
*.cc     text
*.cpp    text
*.h      text
*.hpp    text
*.cmake  text
*.md     text
*.yml    text
*.yaml   text
*.json   text
CMakeLists.txt text
CMakePresets.json text

# Shell scripts must stay LF or they will not execute.
*.sh     text eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts stay CRLF.
*.bat    text eol=crlf
*.cmd    text eol=crlf
*.ps1    text eol=crlf

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Binary -- never convert, never diff
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.ico    binary
*.pdf    binary
*.zip    binary
*.7z     binary
*.dll    binary
*.exe    binary
*.lib    binary
*.pdb    binary
*.bin    binary
*.dat    binary

# Imported compatibility corpora are source artifacts, not Dillen authoring
# files. Preserve their original bytes, encodings, and line endings verbatim.
Dillen-Game/**/corpus/hoi3/** -text

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Vendored third-party sources.
#
# `* text=auto` above would let Git normalise line endings inside SDL, which
# is not ours to decide: upstream ships files whose endings are deliberate and
# whose checksums are published. Marking the tree -text leaves every byte
# exactly as it was cloned, so the vendored copy stays diffable against the
# upstream tag it was pinned at.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Project-Dillen/third_party/** -text
